20:T6ee,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Does this tool confirm that a PAN or GSTIN is active?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. It validates the format only. Use the official Income Tax and GST portals to verify live status."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What does the fourth character of a PAN mean?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It indicates the holder type. For example P is an individual, C a company, H a Hindu Undivided Family and F a firm."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the state code in a GSTIN?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The first two digits identify the state or union territory where the taxpayer is registered, such as 27 for Maharashtra and 29 for Karnataka."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is it safe to type a PAN here?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The check runs in your browser and the number is not stored by us. As a general rule, share your PAN only with parties that need it."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does this verify with the government live?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"This tool checks format and provides official links only. It does not confirm active registration with government databases."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is the PAN / GSTIN Check free on ContentVerse India?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. All India utility tools on ContentVerse India are free to use with no sign-up required."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is this an official government website?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. ContentVerse India is an independent platform. We use public datasets and open APIs. For official records, use government portals like Parivahan, GST, FoSCoS, or ECI."}}]}21:T908,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"HowTo","name":"How to use PAN / GSTIN Check","description":"A PAN (Permanent Account Number) is a 10-character ID issued by the Income Tax Department, and a GSTIN is the 15-character Goods and Services Tax Identification Number issued to registered businesses. This tool validates the format of a PAN or GSTIN and decodes what is inside it: the entity type, th","url":"https://contentverse.co.in/tools/pan-gstin-checker","totalTime":"PT5M","tool":{"@type":"HowToTool","name":"PAN / GSTIN Check"},"step":[{"@type":"HowToStep","position":1,"name":"How to use the PAN / GSTIN checker","text":"Choose the PAN or GSTIN tab, then type or paste the number. The tool checks the length, the pattern of letters and digits, and, for GSTIN, the checksum character. If the format is valid, it shows the decoded details such as the taxpayer type from the fourth character of the PAN and the state from the first two digits of the GSTIN."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":2,"name":"What a PAN tells you","text":"The first three characters are an alphabetic series, the fourth character shows the type of holder, the fifth is usually the first letter of the surname (for individuals) or the entity’s name, followed by four digits and a check letter. The fourth character is useful: P is an individual, C a company, H a Hindu Undivided Family, F a firm, A an association of persons, T a trust, B a body of individuals, L a local authority, J an artificial juridical person and G a government entity."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":3,"name":"How a GSTIN is built","text":"The first two digits are the state code (for example 27 for Maharashtra and 07 for Delhi). The next ten characters are the PAN of the taxpayer. The thirteenth character is the number of registrations the same PAN holds in that state, the fourteenth is the letter Z by default and the fifteenth is a checksum character."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":4,"name":"Format check versus live verification","text":"A format check is offline. It tells you the number is structured correctly but not whether it is registered, cancelled or suspended. The official GST portal’s “Search Taxpayer” and the Income Tax portal’s “Verify PAN” services do that. Use both when the amount involved is significant."}]}16:[[["$","script","0",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"WebApplication\",\"name\":\"PAN / GSTIN Check\",\"alternateName\":\"PAN & GSTIN Format Checker India\",\"description\":\"Validate PAN and GSTIN number format instantly. Decode entity type, state code, and checksum — format check only, not live government verification.\",\"url\":\"https://contentverse.co.in/tools/pan-gstin-checker\",\"applicationCategory\":\"UtilitiesApplication\",\"operatingSystem\":\"Any\",\"browserRequirements\":\"Requires JavaScript\",\"offers\":{\"@type\":\"Offer\",\"price\":\"0\",\"priceCurrency\":\"INR\"},\"provider\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"ContentVerse India\",\"url\":\"https://contentverse.co.in\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-IN\",\"featureList\":\"How to use the PAN / GSTIN checker, What a PAN tells you, How a GSTIN is built, Format check versus live verification\"}"}}],["$","script","1",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$20"}}],["$","script","2",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https://contentverse.co.in\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"India Tools\",\"item\":\"https://contentverse.co.in/tools\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":3,\"name\":\"PAN / GSTIN Check\",\"item\":\"https://contentverse.co.in/tools/pan-gstin-checker\"}]}"}}],["$","script","3",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$21"}}]],"$L22"]
