27:["$","div","What a PAN tells you",{"className":"space-y-3","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-lg font-semibold","children":"What a PAN tells you"}],[["$","p","The first three characters are an alphabetic ser",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base","children":"The first three characters are an alphabetic series, the fourth character shows the type of holder, the fifth is usually the first letter of the surname (for individuals) or the entity’s name, followed by four digits and a check letter. The fourth character is useful: P is an individual, C a company, H a Hindu Undivided Family, F a firm, A an association of persons, T a trust, B a body of individuals, L a local authority, J an artificial juridical person and G a government entity."}],["$","p","For example, a PAN starting ABCPK on the fourth ",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base","children":"For example, a PAN starting ABCPK on the fourth place with P belongs to an individual. If an invoice for a company carries a PAN with the fourth character P, double-check the details."}]],null,null]}]
28:["$","div","How a GSTIN is built",{"className":"space-y-3","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-lg font-semibold","children":"How a GSTIN is built"}],[["$","p","The first two digits are the state code (for exa",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base","children":"The first two digits are the state code (for example 27 for Maharashtra and 07 for Delhi). The next ten characters are the PAN of the taxpayer. The thirteenth character is the number of registrations the same PAN holds in that state, the fourteenth is the letter Z by default and the fifteenth is a checksum character."}],["$","p","Because the PAN is embedded in the GSTIN, you ca",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base","children":"Because the PAN is embedded in the GSTIN, you can cross-check the two. If the PAN on an invoice does not match the middle ten characters of the GSTIN, ask the supplier to correct it before you claim input tax credit."}]],["$","ul",null,{"className":"list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground","children":[["$","li","Check the GSTIN on every B2B invoice before claiming input tax credit",{"children":"Check the GSTIN on every B2B invoice before claiming input tax credit"}],["$","li","Match the supplier’s legal name on the GST portal with the invoice",{"children":"Match the supplier’s legal name on the GST portal with the invoice"}],["$","li","Never share OTPs or passwords with anyone claiming to verify your GST number",{"children":"Never share OTPs or passwords with anyone claiming to verify your GST number"}]]}],null]}]
29:["$","div","Format check versus live verification",{"className":"space-y-3","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-lg font-semibold","children":"Format check versus live verification"}],[["$","p","A format check is offline. It tells you the numb",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground md:text-base","children":"A format check is offline. It tells you the number is structured correctly but not whether it is registered, cancelled or suspended. The official GST portal’s “Search Taxpayer” and the Income Tax portal’s “Verify PAN” services do that. Use both when the amount involved is significant."}]],null,null]}]
